.TH MU2EDAQ-FILE-REAPER-START 1 "2026-09-11" "mu2edaq-file-reaper 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start-mu2edaq-file-reaper.sh \- start the file reaper as a control-room daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start-mu2edaq-file-reaper.sh
[\fICONFIG\fR | \fB\-c\fR \fICONFIG\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIPORT\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-replace\fR]
[\fB\-\-pid\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fIreaper options\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standardised Mu2e control-room start script, run by
.B crs-app start file-reaper
and by hand.  It activates
.IR ./venv ,
stops any copy already running out of the same directory, and executes
.PP
.RS
.nf
python file_reaper.py --config CONFIG --port PORT --daemon --pid-file FILE [options]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Starting is idempotent: a restart never leaves two daemons fighting over the
port.  A running copy is identified both from the PID file and from the
process table (command line mentions
.I file_reaper.py
and the working directory equals the script's directory, checked with
.BR lsof (8)),
so a hand-started copy or one whose PID file vanished is still found, while
an unrelated process that happens to reuse a stale PID is never signalled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.IR CONFIG ", " "\-c \fICONFIG\fR" ", " "\-\-config=\fICONFIG\fR"
Configuration file (default
.IR ./config/mu2edaq-file-reaper.yaml ).
Must exist.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
HTTP port; overrides
.BR CRS_PORT_HTTP .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-replace
Refuse to start (exit 1) if a copy is already running instead of replacing it.
.TP
.BI \-\-pid\-file " FILE"
PID file used both to find a running copy and for the daemon to write
(default
.IR ./file-reaper.pid ).
.TP
Any other option is forwarded to
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper (1)
unchanged, for example
.BR \-\-dry\-run " or " \-\-verbose .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_HTTP
Port exported by the control room from apps.yaml (default 5004).
.TP
.B CRS_STOP_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait after SIGTERM before SIGKILL when replacing a running copy
(default 30).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the daemon was launched; 1 when the configuration file or the virtual
environment is missing, or when
.B \-\-no\-replace
found a running copy; 2 for a malformed option.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I lib/file-reaper-proc.sh
Process discovery shared with the stop script.
.TP
.I ./file-reaper.pid
PID file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper-stop (1),
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper-bootstrap (1),
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper (1)
